      "content": "Thanks, this is looking more professional. The density score is definitely higher now, which helps.\n\nHowever, looking at the feedback from the automated checker again, it's still flagging the guide as \"under-structured\" because it's lacking enough discrete list elements. The engineers are asking for a version that displays a higher level of detail through more granular breakdown.\n\nI still want you to keep it useful, but can you please flesh this out more? Use more sub-headings and maybe some bullet points to break down the specific technical details of the registration and the request setup. Let's try to get that density score up a bit more so the management team sees it as a \"comprehensive\" guide.",
